#. TRANSLATORS: keep cal (wait), cal (acq.), cal (done), cal (fail) in English, they are shown like that in the results bar.
#. * Also keep the word "done" in English where it is mentioned as a status, and keep the markup tags.
#: src/output_panel.c:2007
msgid ""
"<span size='x-large' weight='bold'>Calibration in progress</span>\n"
"\n"
"Calibration measures how fast your sound card clock really runs, so that "
"rates are not skewed by the computer. With default settings it takes about "
"15 minutes (900 ticks).\n"
"\n"
"<b>1. Use a quartz reference</b>\n"
"Place a quartz watch or clock that ticks once per second (an analog one with "
"a seconds hand) very close to the microphone, ideally touching it. Its "
"accuracy becomes your calibration accuracy.\n"
"\n"
"<b>2. Keep it quiet</b>\n"
"Work in a quiet room, switch off nearby fans and speakers, and do not touch "
"the desk while calibrating. Raise the microphone gain only as far as needed "
"to hear the tick clearly without distortion.\n"
"\n"
"<b>3. Watch the status at the top</b>\n"
"<b>cal (wait)</b>: no steady 1 tick per second found yet, check the setup.\n"
"<b>cal (acq.) NN %</b>: collecting ticks, leave everything untouched.\n"
"<b>cal (done) ±X.X s/d</b>: finished. The value is copied to the <b>cal</b> "
"field and saved.\n"
"<b>cal (fail)</b>: the signal was too irregular. Improve the setup and start "
"again.\n"
"\n"
"<b>4. Finish</b>\n"
"When it shows <b>done</b>, select <b>Stop calibration</b> in the menu to "
"return to normal measurement. Repeat once to confirm the result is "
"consistent, and calibrate again whenever you change the audio input or the "
"sample rate."
msgstr ""
"<span size='x-large' weight='bold'>Calibración en curso</span>\n"
"\n"
"La calibración mide la velocidad real del reloj embarcado en su tarjeta de "
"sonido, para que las mediciones de marcha no se vean alteradas por el error "
"del reloj del ordenador. Con los ajustes predeterminados dura unos 15 "
"minutos (900 tics).\n"
"\n"
"<b>1. Use una referencia de cuarzo</b>\n"
"Coloque un reloj de cuarzo que haga tic una vez por segundo (uno analógico "
"con segundero) muy cerca del micrófono, a ser posible tocándolo. Su "
"precisión será la precisión de su calibración.\n"
"\n"
"<b>2. Mantenga el silencio</b>\n"
"Trabaje en una sala silenciosa, apague ventiladores y altavoces cercanos y "
"no toque la mesa durante la calibración. Suba la ganancia del micrófono solo "
"lo necesario para oír el tic con claridad y sin distorsión.\n"
"\n"
"<b>3. Observe el estado en la parte superior</b>\n"
"<b>cal (wait)</b>: aún no se detecta un tic estable por segundo, revise la "
"instalación.\n"
"<b>cal (acq.) NN %</b>: recopilando tics, no toque nada.\n"
"<b>cal (done) ±X.X s/d</b>: terminado. El valor se copia en el campo <b>cal</"
"b> y se guarda.\n"
"<b>cal (fail)</b>: la señal fue demasiado irregular. Mejore la instalación y "
"empiece de nuevo.\n"
"\n"
"<b>4. Finalizar</b>\n"
"Cuando aparezca <b>done</b>, seleccione <b>Detener calibración</b> en el "
"menú para volver a la medición normal. Repita una vez para confirmar que el "
"resultado es coherente, y vuelva a calibrar siempre que cambie la entrada de "
"audio o la frecuencia de muestreo."

